    "text": "A simple pendulum consisting of a mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> attached to a string of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> is released from rest at an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></math>. A pin is located at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> below the pivot point. When the pendulum swings down, the string hits the pin as shown in the figure. If the particle doesn't undergo a complete vertical circle, then the maximum angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;through which the string&nbsp; swings after hitting the pin is<br />\r<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image18-6e54d7d5-2518-4887-a771-07b7585fb11f.jpg\" />",
